**`movedTick(l2Rule, extra)`** CRAP 9.2 (CC 9?): decision points: `extra = extra || {}` (1), `if (extra.items)` (1), for-in (1), `Object.assign(... extra.github || {})` (1), `extra.opts || {}` (1), `if (extra.onCliExecute)` (1), `extra.jobParams || {}` (1) = 7 → CC 8. CRAP 9.2 → coverage slightly less than 100%: CRAP = CC²(1-cov)² + CC → 64(1-cov)² + 8 = 9.2 → (1-cov)² = 1.2/64 = 0.01875 → (1-cov) = 0.1369 → cov ≈ 86%. Fix: extract branches / table merge, or add coverage. Better: simplify structure with a small helper e.g. mergeExtraItems(items, extra) — and cover fully.

**`mergeReservedSlots(jobParams)`** CC 11, CRAP 11 (100% covered). Must reduce CC below... threshold is on CRAP > 8; at full coverage CRAP = CC, so need CC ≤ 8. Refactor:

